{"name":"Santorini Seascape","hex":"#019a8d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seascape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A view of the sea.","A piece of art that depicts the sea or shoreline."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seascape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Santorini","blocks":[{"text":"Santorini, officially Thira or Thera, is a Greek island in the southern Aegean Sea, about 200 km (120 mi) southeast from the mainland. It is the largest island of a small, circular archipelago formed by the Santorini caldera. It is the southernmost member of the Cyclades group of islands, with an area of approximately 73 km2 (28 mi2) and a 2021 census population of 15,480. The municipality of Santorini includes the inhabited islands of Santorini and Therasia, and the uninhabited islands of Nea Kameni, Palaia Kameni, Aspronisi, Anydros, and Christiana. The total land area is 90 km2 (35 mi2). Santorini is part of the Thira regional unit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/2011_Dimos_Thiras.png/330px-2011_Dimos_Thiras.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santorini","wikidata":"Q129296"},{"title":"Seascape","blocks":[{"text":"A seascape is a photograph, painting, or other work of art which depicts the sea, in other words an example of marine art. The word originated as a formation from landscape, which was first used for images of land in art. By a similar development, \"seascape\" has also come to mean actual perceptions of the sea itself. It is applied in planning contexts to geographical locations possessing a good view of the sea. Seascape aesthetics receive legal protection in terms of biodiversity/ health of the seas (the OSPAR Convention, and in terms of the visual bio-cultural seascape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg/330px-The_Wave_-_Pierre-Auguste_Renoir_-_Google_Cultural_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seascape","wikidata":"Q7441810"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Santorini_Montage_L.png/500px-Santorini_Montage_L.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Santorini_Montage_L.png/500px-Santorini_Montage_L.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASantorini_Montage_L.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg/500px-Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg/1280px-Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg/500px-Akrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Springtime landscape in a Fresco from the Bronze Age, Akrotiri","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAkrotiri_Spring_Fresco_room.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg/330px-Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg/330px-Saffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"saffron-gatherers\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaffron_gatherersSantorini-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"h